              <subFactors xsi:type="dssmmDiffMM:DiffLeafFactor" FactorID="196624" Name="Move, queue, setup, and run times can be scheduled for sequential and overlapping operations" Descr="Operations can be scheduled so they can accommodate sequential and overlapping operations. A sequential operation is one where a work center can run jobs one after the other. An overlapping operation is one which begins a new sublot (e.g., sublot B) before the first sublot (e.g., sublot A) is complete. Sublot A is sent to the second stage of the operation once it is completed, allowing sublot B to enter the first stage. Both of these operations are designed to maximize capacity constraints in order to meet order deadlines." GW="1.53E-4" LW="0.076923" Hierarchy="3.2.4.3" MasterFactorID="196624" diff_kind_Right="DELETE">
