          <subFactors xsi:type="dssmmDiffMM:DiffCompositeFactor" FactorID="198123" Name="Online Requirements for Purchasing Management" Descr="Online tools and portals are increasingly used by organizations for supplier interactions. In order to make communication efficient for both parties, these tools should provide functionality such as information on all available suppliers; the possibility of creating purchase orders with advanced options (e.g., define frequency, define delivery method, define payment methods, etc); collaboration that will allow changes to be easily communicated to suppliers, etc.)." GW="0.010417" LW="0.083333" Hierarchy="5.11" MasterFactorID="198123" diff_kind_Left="MODIFY" diff_kind_Right="DELETE" changeStatus="CONTRADICTING" new_Hierarchy_Left="4.11"/>
          <subFactors xsi:type="dssmmDiffMM:DiffCompositeFactor" FactorID="198092" Name="Receipts for Procurement" Descr="Receipts for procurement refers to the criteria related to the reception of ordered goods from the supplier. Between the moment when goods arrive and the moment when they are physically stored in the warehouse, there are a few factors that need to be taken into consideration, such as the quantity of the good received (Does it correspond to the quantity ordered?); the quality of the goods (Were the goods damaged during transportation or handling? Did perishable goods expire before getting shipped?); and pricing (Did the price of the goods delivered change due to unexpected factors?)." GW="0.010417" LW="0.083333" Hierarchy="5.10" MasterFactorID="198092" diff_kind_Right="DELETE">
            <scores xsi:type="dssmmDiffMM:DiffScore" Descr="91.0" Comment="" score_option="/0/@options.0" diff_kind_Right="DELETE">
