        <subFactors xsi:type="dssmmDiffMM:DiffCompositeFactor" FactorID="198157" Name="Quality Management" Descr="Quality management refers to the set of actions taken by an organization to ensure that it creates and delivers high-quality products. In order to do so, organizations must comply to national and international rules and regulations related to product quality, but they often also create and use internal requirements for quality control. Specific procedures need to be set up in order to ensure that the end products comply to internal or external quality standards. All these activities need to be well documented in order to provide the information needed when customers are not satisfied with the quality of the products received. Government agencies may also require this information for control and verification." GW="0.125" LW="0.125" Hierarchy="6" MasterFactorID="198157" diff_kind_Right="DELETE"/>
        <subFactors xsi:type="dssmmDiffMM:DiffCompositeFactor" FactorID="196138" Name="Human Resources" Descr="Human Resources encompasses all the applications necessary for handling personnel-related tasks for corporate managers and individual employees. Modules will include Personnel Management, Benefit Management, Payroll Management, Employee Self Service, Data Warehousing, Health and Safety, Workforce Management, Training, and Product Technology" GW="0.125" LW="0.125" Hierarchy="2" MasterFactorID="196138" diff_kind_Left="MODIFY" new_LW_Left="0.109375"/>
        <subFactors xsi:type="dssmmDiffMM:DiffCompositeFactor" FactorID="198157" Name="Quality Management" Descr="Quality management refers to the set of actions taken by an organization to ensure that it creates and delivers high-quality products. In order to do so, organizations must comply to national and international rules and regulations related to product quality, but they often also create and use internal requirements for quality control. Specific procedures need to be set up in order to ensure that the end products comply to internal or external quality standards. All these activities need to be well documented in order to provide the information needed when customers are not satisfied with the quality of the products received. Government agencies may also require this information for control and verification." GW="0.125" LW="0.125" Hierarchy="6" MasterFactorID="198157" diff_kind_Left="MODIFY" new_LW_Left="0.5"/>
